{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152441Z","id":"55f28ea7aa42e20647411e816c07f9f2f4f97bb695ec0768a124dea6a1fa9981","body":{"detail":"Why it cannot be forged: claxHost exists only in app mode (installHost, loaded by web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts:18 for ?app=1), on the top-level shell window. The content frame is cross-origin (subdomain mode) or an opaque origin (sandbox mode), so parent.claxHost / top.claxHost throw SecurityError there (web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts 'the page cannot reach claxHost', both modes). No frame message calls it: the host's own listener takes only clax:scroll (web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'nothing the page posts attests a finger'). The Flutter host reaches it by runJavaScript, which runs in the main frame. Outside app mode hostArrival.fresh stays false (web/shell/src/caps/gesture.ts:561; test 'is not counted outside app mode, nor after uninstall'). Accepted residual: an attestation stands in only for condition 3 of frameGesture (activation and focus in the frame still required), counts only after the latest shell input and for ATTEST_MS (1 s, line 61), and only when elementFromPoint(x, y) is the frame (not a shell control over it). Within that second after the viewer's real touch on the page, a hostile page can have a composer-tier or strict-tier call counted: the same residual as a real click in the page (gesture.ts header). The host must attest only pointers that reach the WebView (not Flutter widgets drawn over it), in CSS pixels of the WebView viewport, on both press and release (a pick can come up to ~400 ms after the release, web/bridge/src/comment-mode.ts TOUCH_CLICK_WAIT_MS).","kind":"waiver","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":230},"content_hash":"7013134a34a56e4bc6f5ea0ebb9b9e192ecd2ebe1d018d8bb83173844be0c48a"},"summary":"A host attestation counts as the finger's arrival on the frame: trusted only because nothing but the shell's own document can call it","tags":["security","gesture","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T07:22:41.152658Z","id":"2e2c5abc5f65e00f4ecc2d42cacb4ea8578db382d6a8e15994af254eba199284","body":{"detail":"follow() reports FOLLOW_FAILED and returns; it runs again from the state subscription (any change while newer is set) or from claxHost.reloadLatest(). There is no timed retry, so with a quiet view a transient daemon failure leaves the older version shown with the notice until something else changes. The app's host can call reloadLatest on the notice.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":121},"end":{"line":130},"content_hash":"2f56f0c5189689012dbc4373106431447bae385cc5757ae69efc6538addebaf9"},"summary":"A failed auto-follow fetch is retried only on the view's next state change","tags":["app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:17:07.648054Z","id":"1bd057916e9e0edf520e7db1bfb56fc6b07493a9a411bda98c286245e0917f1c","body":{"detail":"Failure: /a/<id>?app=1 where the served frame's clax:hello is handled (replayed from __claxEarly at mount, web/shell/src/artifact-main.ts:15) before import('./app/host') resolves (artifact-main.ts:18). ArtifactController welcomes synchronously (artifact-controller.ts:1120) with ctl.app still null: no `ready` is posted for that page (the say->usable timer, spec 6.1 step 3, never stops) and the welcome lacks app: true, so the bridge sends no clax:scroll and the first auto-follow lands at the top instead of the kept scroll (spec 6.2 step 5). Measured with a Playwright probe at 390x800 against a scratch daemon, the host-*.js request delayed by 30 ms: 1 of 2 loads had no ready and 0 clax:scroll reports; delayed 100 ms: 1 of 2; no delay: 10 of 10 fine. The margin is tens of milliseconds, and a phone's WebView is slower than desktop Chromium. No test installs the host after a hello.","kind":"blocker","span":{"start":{"line":75},"end":{"line":96},"content_hash":"cbb24bfed60550843fb9741968bf486bcbb7b7da3956d5ffb5fa21546270ec76"},"suggested_fix":"In installHost, when a page already greeted (ctl.state.get().file !== null), send the frame clax:greet (web/bridge/src/protocol.ts:69) so it greets again and gets ready plus a welcome with app: true; add a host.test.ts case that installs after hello(frame).","summary":"A page that greets before the lazy host chunk loads gets no ready and no app: true welcome","tags":["review","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:17:07.648150Z","id":"03bd3e00980f4c8c048b07f833f97f636d649937a513e1e382c12d0151f3b387","body":{"detail":"webview_flutter_android 4.14.1 registers channels with addJavascriptInterface (WebViewProxyApi.java:249), which Android exposes in all frames including cross-origin iframes; webview_flutter_wkwebview 3.27.0 injects window.<name> with isForMainFrameOnly: false (webkit_webview_controller.dart:438). So the framed page can call window.ClaxHost.postMessage with a forged `state` carrying a draft (spec 3.7: the app then starts dictation, turning on the microphone), forged `sent`/`landed` (Working chip and long-press->landed timing), `ready` (say->usable timing), `notice` and `threads` (spoofed panel). The shell side cannot stop this alone.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":82},"end":{"line":85},"content_hash":"ed9b3e5834daa125b519e2ed060145db73ea0a48e831850a02766a11463332fd"},"suggested_fix":"Authenticate the shell's messages: the host hands the shell a per-load nonce by runJavaScript (e.g. claxHost.bind(nonce)), the shell adds it to every HostMessage, and the host (plan Task F8, host_protocol.dart) drops messages without it, including any before bind.","summary":"The artifact page can post any HostMessage: the ClaxHost channel is injected into every frame","tags":["review","security","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:17:07.648187Z","id":"6cb6278cb7dc738f913da7057cacb34971b00f759d596f7ea6205a002a6f15f9","body":{"detail":"The host's runJavaScript arrives after the WebView handled the touch. A tap on the composer's Cancel or Send, or a notice's Dismiss, closes that control on click; the release's attestation then finds the frame under (x, y), and attestedAt is later than the click's lastShellInputAt, so hostArrival.fresh holds for ATTEST_MS. With the shell's activation from that click and focus in the frame (the page can pull it, gesture.ts residual), the page has a composer-tier gesture for 1 s: a forged pick or a prefilled composer, on which the app starts dictation. The strict tier stays blocked by SHELL_QUIET_MS (5.5 s). This is the layout-change case that gesture.ts's arrival rules close for Chromium's mouseover.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":229},"content_hash":"d2d2001d343af89684a93777a5927418ecd5acf02d547bc3e4e59146d76e7997"},"suggested_fix":"Count a release only when the press of the same pointer was attested on the frame (attestPointer takes a pointer ID and down/up), and drop the pair when the press landed on a shell control.","summary":"An attestation is hit-tested when its script runs, not when the finger moved: a release on a shell control that has since vanished counts as a finger on the frame","tags":["review","security","gesture","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:17:07.648219Z","id":"8de86523d3fa5ef637ca507da016a4b19140da3df39ddf48a7a44419279d04a4","body":{"detail":"The app calls window.claxHost?.… by runJavaScript in the WebView's main frame. The content sandbox allows popups (crates/clax-server/src/routes/content.rs:24), and an Android WebView without multiple-window support may load a window.open or target=_blank URL in the same WebView; the plan's NavigationDelegate for Task F8 allows the daemon's origin and *.localhost, which includes the subdomain content origin. An artifact loaded top-level can define its own window.claxHost and receive setDraftText (the viewer's dictated words) and attestations.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":38},"end":{"line":56},"content_hash":"431e967ce680a0b89328672fcc7d6eee719cbd5ed223b6a6ccdd7e9a98706812"},"suggested_fix":"F8: allow top-level navigation only to the daemon origin's /a/<id>[/v/<n>]?app=1 shell paths (open anything else outside the app), and send claxHost calls only while the WebView's URL is such a path; cover it in the F10 integration test.","summary":"The host's claxHost calls reach whatever document is top-level, including an artifact page loaded there","tags":["review","security","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T08:17:07.648249Z","id":"f86fc1eed4948be12e808b699691950cf8649b7e3e19548a3e7bc572260ab6e2","body":{"detail":"The composer has closed and the thread exists with sent_to_agent false; the host gets `notice` and a `threads` entry with sent: false, but ClaxHost has no call to send a thread, and app.css hides the sidebar whose Send button would. The comment never reaches the agent.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":108},"end":{"line":115},"content_hash":"0aa7e40901e70df988ff553d7bf3f2527431904535fe9e7786a3dd362a0ae031"},"suggested_fix":"Add claxHost.sendThread(id) (sendToAgent with the view's sendTo, then `sent`), so the panel can offer Send again on a thread with sent: false.","summary":"A Send whose post succeeded but whose send failed leaves the thread unsent, with no way to resend it from the app","tags":["review","app-mode","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:26.107572Z","id":"f2e0d76fee72e082c67ce8aec3319b5b31ba46c9ed6c7422d4011b990313a264","body":{"detail":"Shell side (commit 130e2614): installHost runs only in the top-level document at /a/<id>[/v/<n>][/<file>] with app=1 (host.ts:120). It posts nothing on window.ClaxHost until claxHost.init({nonce}) with a nonce matching ^[A-Za-z0-9_-]{16,128}$; the first valid init wins, later ones are ignored. init posts the current state, threads, and the latest page's ready; every message from then on is the HostMessage plus nonce (type Posted). App side (F8, host_protocol.dart): for every load of the shell document (onPageFinished of a main-frame /a/...?app=1 URL), make a fresh random nonce (at least 128 bits, base64url), call window.claxHost.init({nonce}) by runJavaScript once claxHost exists (it arrives with a lazy chunk: retry until typeof window.claxHost === 'object'), and drop every channel message whose nonce is not that load's, including all messages before init. The channel is injected into every frame (Android addJavascriptInterface, WKWebView isForMainFrameOnly: false), so the artifact's page can post on it; it cannot learn the nonce: the shell document is cross-origin to the page (subdomain origin, or opaque in sandbox mode) and never posts the nonce to the frame (web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'posts nothing before init...', web/e2e/app-mode.spec.ts 'the page cannot reach claxHost', both frame modes).","kind":"comment","span":{"start":{"line":20},"end":{"line":37},"content_hash":"12e78e07db5ab875fa1c32a0fe6b258f1701e6001ffcb5f7dd319d998a4b5ae6"},"summary":"The ClaxHost channel protocol the app (plan Task F8) must implement: per-load nonce via claxHost.init, nothing before it, nonce on every message, drop the rest","tags":["protocol","security","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:26.107732Z","id":"28bdd575a6a1e6efea5146e18d6cc6fed446098f5dc6ad70640c50d2f7449298","body":{"detail":"F8 (NavigationDelegate) must: (1) allow a main-frame navigation only when its URL has the daemon's exact origin (http://127.0.0.1:<port>, not *.localhost) and path /a/<12-char id>, optionally /v/<n> and a file path, with app=1 in the query; open every other main-frame URL outside the app (url_launcher) or block it; subframe navigations (the content frame, *.localhost subdomain origins) stay allowed; (2) refuse new windows (window.open, target=_blank) in the WebView; (3) before any claxHost call (runJavaScript), check the WebView's current URL still meets (1), and re-init the nonce after each such page load. F10's integration test should cover a page that window.open()s and navigates top to its own URL.","kind":"comment","references":"8de86523d3fa5ef637ca507da016a4b19140da3df39ddf48a7a44419279d04a4","summary":"Shell side done in 130e2614 (no claxHost outside the top-level /a/...?app=1 document); the navigation rule F8 must enforce is below","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:26.107929Z","id":"bf9046bc10b93a0a6297726d642c6f992b76372d2f416de955b84d74e0466ac4","body":{"detail":"The press is hit-tested with elementFromPoint when its script runs; a release counts only for a pointer whose press so counted, so a tap on a shell control that closes on click (Cancel, Send, Dismiss) never attests the frame. Test: web/shell/src/app/host.test.ts 'counts a release only when the same pointer's press was attested on the frame'. F8 must send the platform pointer ID and phase for each down and up.","kind":"comment","references":"55f28ea7aa42e20647411e816c07f9f2f4f97bb695ec0768a124dea6a1fa9981","span":{"start":{"line":221},"end":{"line":230},"content_hash":"7b91a5e5a6ad198f30b9abe4fd9c954453387e69d31447592c9d30dd3c1f01f6"},"summary":"Since 130e2614 attestPointer takes {pointer, phase}: a release counts only when the same pointer's press was hit-tested on the frame","tags":["session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:43.296921Z","id":"aba6f1d4dfc2c633dd82134fd89e9f1585db6a38b76f12a40daa1b51ffaa6bd5","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:130e2614","summary":"Fixed: installHost sends clax:greet when the gate is open; host.test.ts 'a page that greeted before the host loaded is asked to greet again...' passes, and e2e/app-mode.spec.ts 'a page that greets before the host module loads still gets ready and app mode' (host chunk held until the page's hello) passed 3/3 repeats in both frame modes","supersedes":"1bd057916e9e0edf520e7db1bfb56fc6b07493a9a411bda98c286245e0917f1c","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:43.550451Z","id":"2af67ce11f0bc9fa7f24488c532659178a9d9750210d3112f9aa20086dc87258","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:130e2614","summary":"Fixed on the shell side: claxHost.init({nonce}), nothing posted before it, nonce on every message (host.test.ts 'posts nothing before init...', 'ignores an init without a well-formed nonce'; e2e 'the page cannot reach claxHost' checks the frame never hears it). The app's half (drop messages without the nonce) is specified for F8 in the protocol record on host.ts:20:37","supersedes":"03bd3e00980f4c8c048b07f833f97f636d649937a513e1e382c12d0151f3b387","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:43.672311Z","id":"36b5a7ba018016848697d86433190624d657d9cdc7c08cc9bbc2b1b93fa3e694","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:130e2614","summary":"Fixed: attestPointer takes {pointer, phase}; a release counts only when that pointer's press was hit-tested on the frame (host.test.ts 'counts a release only when the same pointer's press was attested on the frame' passes)","supersedes":"6cb6278cb7dc738f913da7057cacb34971b00f759d596f7ea6205a002a6f15f9","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"web/shell/src/app/host.ts","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-12T09:47:43.851531Z","id":"c5a550b4324857ccaf05fcfcd64d14d5fab6a9d88d9e759d8704557d2217c99a","body":{"kind":"resolve","ref":"git:130e2614","summary":"Fixed: claxHost.resend(id) sends an open unsent thread, and a failed send posts sendFailed {thread, text} (host.test.ts 'a failed send posts sendFailed, and resend sends the thread' passes)","supersedes":"f86fc1eed4948be12e808b699691950cf8649b7e3e19548a3e7bc572260ab6e2","tags":["reason:fixed","session:claude-code:e697d918-f48a-41f9-aac4-4be74128e8ae"]}}
